gitcha (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Apache Cassandra as the database (GITCHA_STORE=cassandra), the build
    option on by default: rows per entry, one atomic batch per change, a
    lease so one server owns an instance, a check of the secret key, and a
    one-time import of an existing db.json.  --without-cassandra (the build
    profile pkg.gitcha.nocassandra) leaves the driver out.
  * Full Debian packaging (debian/, deploy/build-debian.sh) with debconf, a
    preseed example, a signed apt repository builder (deploy/apt-repo.sh) and
    deploy/mass-install.sh for many hosts over SSH.
  * Reverse proxy examples for Caddy, nginx, Apache httpd and HAProxy, and
    how to run without a proxy on a trusted network.
  * Versions are now X.Y.Z+gitYYYYMMDDHHMMSS.<sha7>: the commit's time comes
    before its hash, so apt always sees a newer commit as newer.  The old
    X.Y.Z+git<sha7> sorted by the hash's letters and could hide an upgrade;
    the move to 0.2.0 puts every new build above the old ones.
  * A third package, inputloop-gitcha-medic: a timer that looks at Gitcha, its
    Cassandra and its proxy, says what is wrong and why, runs the safe remedies
    when told it may, parks the rest for a person (--yes NAME), and tells
    syslog, Tavern, chadgram, a webhook or a C4 folder.  An agent (the Claude
    API; local and inputloop vendors reserved) can be asked for a second
    opinion over redacted facts.
  * A fourth package, inputloop-gitcha-omni-gateway: the stdio MCP servers a
    host runs (vibrobeast's memory seat and persona sheets, Tavern, Gitcha)
    behind HTTP on loopback, one URL and one bearer token per member, each
    run as the user whose files it serves, for a Claude session in a cloud
    sandbox to reach through the omni plugin; nginx with TLS goes in front.
    The medic watches it.

 -- inputloop <nathanielfrankford@gmail.com>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:30:00 +0000

gitcha (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Full Debian packaging (debian/, dpkg-buildpackage): debconf questions so
    a preseed file installs and configures Gitcha with no prompts, an apt
    repository builder, and a mass-install script for many hosts.
  * Apache Cassandra as the database, the build option on by default; the
    build profile pkg.gitcha.nocassandra leaves it out (db.json instead).

 -- inputloop <nathanielfrankford@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
